Falsifies `system_tests::user::process_tests::two_threads_of_one_process_share_its_space_its_table_and_a_futex`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect, in milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one address space)'s process object: a thread that joins a process keeps its own capability
table instead of taking the process's, so siblings share a space and not their authority.

Expected to fail: "the waker's WAKE through the shared slot 0 woke nobody". The waker's slot 0 is
empty, so its `WAKE` answers `NoSuchSlot`.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched/process.rs b/kernel/src/sched/process.rs
--- a/kernel/src/sched/process.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched/process.rs
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ pub(super) fn join(
             }
         }
         (*ptr).process = Some(pid);
-        (*ptr).capability_table = table_at(phys);
+        let _ = phys;
     }
     process.members += 1;
     Ok(space)
